# dbus FHS migration: system bus runtime /run/dbus -> /var/run/dbus.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - Socket: the daemon does not reclaim a stale socket file (bind
#   fails on an existing path). The OpenRC start_pre removes
#   /var/run/dbus/system_bus_socket when starting (runs only when
#   OpenRC is about to start the daemon); the systemd socket unit
#   binds -- and reclaims -- the socket itself. Ownership of stale
#   cleanup therefore lives in service logic, never in this fragment.
# - New /var/run/dbus: converged here on upgrade (messagebus:81);
#   created by checkpath/socket unit on fresh installs.
# - Old /run/dbus: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once empty
#   (old daemon gone, socket file gone with reboot or cleanup);
#   left in place and reported while occupied.

dir /var/run/dbus 0755 messagebus messagebus
rmdir-if-empty /run/dbus
